1
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:09,650
Our little Hotaru's really gone
and become someone's girlfriend now.

2
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:15,600
Congratulations again, Hotaru.

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,940
I'm so happy for you!

4
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:21,720
The only reason someone like me
was able to fall in love

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:24,790
is because I got so much good 
advice from the two of you.

6
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:26,320
Thank you so much.

7
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:32,380
So, what are you two going to do during 
spring break? Go on a bunch of dates?

8
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,220
Hmm...

9
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,030
But we see each other all the time at work.

10
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:39,700
Huh?

11
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:44,390
Hananoi-kun got a job
 at the place where I work.

12
00:00:44,390 --> 00:00:45,390
Huh?!

13
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:51,080
Hotaru-chan, I want to ask you something.

14
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:53,960
Um...

15
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:01,820
If it's okay with you, Hotaru-chan,

16
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,090
I want to spend more time together.

17
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:12,580
I-I wasn't so sure about it either, but he 
promised to keep it professional at work.

18
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,750
Well, as long as you're okay with it.

19
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:17,590
Still, you should try
 to maintain a <i>little</i> distance.

20
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:22,630
I mean, can someone like him 
who has zero interest in strangers

21
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:25,460
even work a customer service job?

22
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:04,700
Episode 8

23
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:04,700
My First Pet

24
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,190
<i>Zero interest in strangers, huh?</i>

25
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,930
<i>I guess I kind of knew that...</i>

26
00:03:05,690 --> 00:03:11,180
<i>But it hasn't caused problems so far,
and everyone here's real nice.</i>

27
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,710
<i>Everything should be fine, right?</i>

28
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:15,360
Um, Hananoi-kun!

29
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,180
Can I please take your picture?!

30
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,680
No way.

31
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:24,070
<i>E-Everyone really is nice...</i>

32
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:27,180
Oh, Hotaru-chan! Good morning.

33
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,410
G-Good morning.

34
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,260
<i>Gosh, I'm still not used to this!</i>

35
00:03:34,970 --> 00:03:36,950
That covers it for now.

36
00:03:37,270 --> 00:03:39,820
Okay, let's make this another great day.

37
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:41,230
We'll do our best!

38
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:45,050
Oh, Hananoi, come with me.

39
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:50,060
And that's how it's done. You get all that?

40
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,010
Yes.

41
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:55,510
The register should be your priority,
so just come out on the floor when you can.

42
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:57,590
You won't get to this all.

43
00:03:57,590 --> 00:03:58,360
All right.

44
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:04,770
I heard that you're Hinase-san's 
boyfriend. Is that right?

45
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:07,480
Yes, that's correct.

46
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:12,650
Well, try not to show it 
when you're on the job, okay?

47
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:16,270
You two are here to work, after all.

48
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:25,480
I give thanks to this lovely 
world and to Hota-chan!

49
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:29,660
I still can't believe you two
get to work together.

50
00:04:30,290 --> 00:04:34,390
I'm so jealous! I never had anything
like that when I was younger.

51
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:36,850
Even Yao-kun is super popular.

52
00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:40,260
Please stop talking like I get all the girls.

53
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,460
I haven't had much luck
 when it comes to romance.

54
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:48,200
Still, I have more respect for people 
who take good care of their friends,

55
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,350
even if they've never been in love.

56
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:58,980
The manager asked if you could bundle
 these magazines together.

57
00:04:58,980 --> 00:04:59,980
Roger that.

58
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,500
H-Hananoi-kun?

59
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,030
<i>O-Oh, that's right.</i>

60
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:12,820
<i>I was worried about things 
between him and Yao-kun...</i>

61
00:05:15,230 --> 00:05:17,470
<i>But all seems well now, I suppose.</i>

62
00:05:19,850 --> 00:05:20,800
Oh.

63
00:05:23,310 --> 00:05:24,640
Good work today.

64
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:31,780
<i>Guess he's dropped the act now.</i>

65
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:37,060
Hey, I know I made a bad 
impression when we met,

66
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:39,910
but Hotako and I are just friends.

67
00:05:39,910 --> 00:05:43,320
Since we're working together now, 
let's try to get along, okay?

68
00:05:44,670 --> 00:05:48,310
Would you knock it off
with the "Hotako" stuff?

69
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:53,340
I don't know about your past, but you don't look 
like you're even much "friends" anymore to me.

70
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,450
Stay away from Hotaru-chan, okay?

71
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:05,840
Yeesh, I don't think he likes me.

72
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:11,490
Hananoi-kun! Thanks for waiting.

73
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:14,610
Good job today, Hotaru-chan.

74
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:19,280
How are you getting along with Manager Kuroe?

75
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,330
Hmm...

76
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:24,240
As long as I'm with you, it's all good.

77
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:27,870
<i>That must mean there's been some friction.</i>

78
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:31,260
<i>Manager Kuroe </i>can<i> be pretty strict.</i>

79
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:35,630
<i>Maybe I can help smooth things over. 
I'll have to keep an eye on things.</i>

80
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:40,200
By the way, Hananoi-kun, do you want 
to go to a cafe or something?

81
00:06:43,390 --> 00:06:49,500
And so, now that we're officially dating, 
let's discuss our policies going forward!

82
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,910
Policies?

83
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:57,630
Like we discussed the other day, we each
have what's important to us in a relationship.

84
00:06:57,630 --> 00:07:03,020
So if you don't mind, can you maybe tell me
things you wouldn't want me to do?

85
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:08,600
I may not be able to honor everything, 
but just like there are things we want to do,

86
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,540
it's important to be on the same page
about what we don't want.

87
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:15,420
This is kind of sudden...

88
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,680
What about you?

89
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,740
Me?

90
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,740
I, well...

91
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:22,490
Um...

92
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:24,900
I dunno...

93
00:07:25,790 --> 00:07:30,150
Let me think. Things I don't want you to do...

94
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:35,510
I don't want you to leave 
me behind, I guess.

95
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:36,630
Huh?

96
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:40,540
Yeah. I don't want you to leave me behind.

97
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:45,770
We are now closed for the day.

98
00:07:46,350 --> 00:07:49,170
I can finally get started 
on restocking the shelves.

99
00:07:49,670 --> 00:07:50,520
Hmm?

100
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,600
It's already done.

101
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,380
Good evening—

102
00:07:58,380 --> 00:07:59,150
Oh!

103
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:02,120
Wh-What's all this?

104
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:07,710
Well, we got a huge order of dictionaries 
for new elementary school students.

105
00:08:07,710 --> 00:08:13,260
They have to be delivered soon, so I guess 
I'll stay late after closing to wrap them all.

106
00:08:13,690 --> 00:08:15,900
We'd like to help!

107
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:18,830
We can do them bit by bit 
during business hours.

108
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,530
Thanks. That'd be a huge help.

109
00:08:23,530 --> 00:08:25,210
Then it's settled!

110
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:28,950
You guys can show off the 
wrapping skills you've practiced!

111
00:08:28,950 --> 00:08:29,850
Yeah!

112
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:43,080
We are now closed for the day.

113
00:08:41,670 --> 00:08:46,090
You're kidding me. You did all 
this with just the three of you?

114
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:50,620
We're experts at a quick,
 clean wrapping job now.

115
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,580
Plus, it was the four of us!

116
00:08:52,970 --> 00:08:54,300
Hananoi-kun helped too!

117
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:55,730
Huh...

118
00:08:56,600 --> 00:09:00,310
But Hananoi just started here. 
He hasn't learned how to wrap yet.

119
00:09:00,610 --> 00:09:04,780
He said he watched other people 
doing it and practiced at home.

120
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:09,440
U-Um, Hananoi-kun is always like that!

121
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,380
I guess you could say he's a good student.

122
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:16,690
Good work again today.

123
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:19,360
You can call it a night.

124
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,380
All right.

125
00:09:23,650 --> 00:09:26,230
You sure are something.

126
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:29,720
You're just a part-timer.
Why are you putting in so much effort?

127
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:34,560
I don't care what you think of me,

128
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:37,660
but I don't want to make Hinase-san look bad.

129
00:09:38,090 --> 00:09:40,530
What does that mean?

130
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:43,300
I don't think you like me very much, Manager.

131
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:46,150
Huh? Why would you say—

132
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:46,800
Oh.

133
00:09:47,590 --> 00:09:51,110
You two are here to work, after all.

134
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:53,660
Ah...

135
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:57,900
Okay, sorry. That was my bad.
 I was out of line.

136
00:09:59,090 --> 00:10:01,900
It's not like... I mean...

137
00:10:02,490 --> 00:10:06,400
Supervising a regular customer
 is just awkward for me.

138
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:10,050
I wasn't sure how to treat you, I guess.

139
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:14,570
You used to shop here all the time, right?

140
00:10:15,230 --> 00:10:21,120
You always bought the books I made 
displays for, so I remember you.

141
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,270
Boy, I sure am exhausted today!

142
00:10:25,850 --> 00:10:30,010
But Manager Kuroe gave me cocoa as thanks.

143
00:10:30,010 --> 00:10:31,930
He gave me a coffee.

144
00:10:31,930 --> 00:10:35,520
I got it in my head that he was kind of 
scary, but he's actually nice.

145
00:10:37,390 --> 00:10:38,270
Yeah.

146
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:42,430
Oh... Are you still having trouble 
getting along with him?

147
00:10:42,430 --> 00:10:44,790
No, well...

148
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:51,800
Just that Kuroe-san remembers that I've been
 frequenting the store since a long time ago.

149
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,620
It's kind of... embarrassing.

150
00:10:57,820 --> 00:11:01,620
<i>He... He's blushing?! Hananoi-kun's blushing!</i>

151
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:06,260
<i>I'm glad I said I didn't mind
 working together.</i>

152
00:11:06,950 --> 00:11:08,690
<i>Regardless of the reason,</i>

153
00:11:09,050 --> 00:11:12,920
<i>it can't be a bad thing for Hananoi-kun 
to open himself up to new things, right?</i>

154
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:16,190
Is something wrong?

155
00:11:16,470 --> 00:11:17,550
Nope!

156
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:23,150
Oh, the bus is here.

157
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:27,130
Okay, Hananoi-kun. See you tomorrow!

158
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:31,080
I want to stay with you...

159
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:33,290
just a little longer.

160
00:11:42,350 --> 00:11:45,840
I'm glad that I get to spend
 more time with you,

161
00:11:46,370 --> 00:11:49,620
but I can't really touch 
you unless we're alone.

162
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:51,420
I-I guess you're right.

163
00:12:03,730 --> 00:12:06,000
H-Hananoi-kun?

164
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:10,960
I figure if we do this more,
you'll get used to it.

165
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:15,440
What? I don't know if
 I'll ever get used to this!

166
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:21,330
It feels like ever since 
you told me you liked me,

167
00:12:21,330 --> 00:12:22,620
I've been walking on air.

168
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:26,880
Me too. I've been walking 
on air this whole time.

169
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,510
One day,

170
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:36,340
when we finally share a real kiss,

171
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:40,360
I want you to be as elated as I will be.

172
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:46,790
So when your heart is ready for it
and you decide you want it,

173
00:12:46,790 --> 00:12:48,230
give me a signal, okay?

174
00:12:50,170 --> 00:12:53,200
<i>I can't even imagine it yet,</i>

175
00:12:53,990 --> 00:12:59,030
<i>but if we both keep doing things 
at our own pace... that works, right?</i>

176
00:13:01,010 --> 00:13:05,040
Huh? Keigo-kun invited you
 over to his house, Kyo-chan?

177
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:07,810
<i>Yeah. This is actually the first time.</i>

178
00:13:07,810 --> 00:13:10,810
But listen, Kei-chan says...

179
00:13:10,810 --> 00:13:15,510
that his family has an absolutely
giant golden retriever!

180
00:13:15,510 --> 00:13:17,020
Whoa!

181
00:13:18,370 --> 00:13:23,930
And so that's why I wanted to ask you, 
Yao-kun. Since you have a dog,

182
00:13:23,930 --> 00:13:26,760
you must know a few tricks 
for befriending them.

183
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:28,580
Tricks, huh?

184
00:13:29,590 --> 00:13:30,610
Oh.

185
00:13:30,610 --> 00:13:32,080
Well, why don't you just come over?

186
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,520
Where'd that come from?

187
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:38,050
I mean, won't it help to actually
 spend time with a dog?

188
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:40,690
You can come too, Hananoi.

189
00:13:43,050 --> 00:13:46,120
Do you mind if I check with my friend first?

190
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,870
Kyo-chan, we haven't made it to the dog yet.

191
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:54,530
Just leave me here and go on without me!

192
00:13:55,610 --> 00:13:57,850
Okay, but please make sure you come.

193
00:13:57,850 --> 00:13:59,310
Mm-hmm.

194
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:02,810
Sorry to drag you along.

195
00:14:02,810 --> 00:14:06,330
Are you okay with this? 
I mean, with Yao-kun and all.

196
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:07,800
It'll be fine.

197
00:14:08,310 --> 00:14:11,580
But are <i>you</i> okay with this, Hotaru-chan?

198
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:15,840
I thought that you were avoiding Yao-kun.

199
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,910
Huh? Why?

200
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:20,890
Was I acting strange or something?

201
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:25,880
I wasn't trying to avoid him.

202
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:31,510
Um, Yao-kun and I go way back,
so things <i>are</i> a little awkward.

203
00:14:32,150 --> 00:14:34,840
But today's a special opportunity.

204
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:38,970
If it's to help Kyo-chan,
I'll do whatever I can.

205
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:43,360
Thanks for having us... over!

206
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,450
We're coming in.

207
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:49,970
Oh! Is that Hotaru?

208
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:55,080
I dunno. Maybe it's just the name,
but doesn't she kinda look like you?

209
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:55,870
Huh?

210
00:14:55,870 --> 00:14:59,670
I know what you mean.
 They have the exact same eyebrows.

211
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:05,370
Yao-kun, weren't you Hotaru's classmate
in elementary school?

212
00:15:05,370 --> 00:15:07,500
Yup. Class 1 in sixth grade.

213
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,280
I met her in the second year of junior high.

214
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:14,150
I bet in middle school, Hota—
Um, what was Hinase like then?

215
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:17,390
Hmm, she was basically the same.

216
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:16,830
<i>Huh? What did he just call me?</i>

217
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:21,280
She was a little quieter back then. 
Like she kept her guard up, I guess?

218
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,000
Huh?

219
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,110
Yeah, I was real shocked when I heard
you used to have guy friends like Yao-kun!

220
00:15:26,110 --> 00:15:29,500
K-Kyo-chan, that's ancient history.

221
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:32,460
She was quiet in elementary school too.

222
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:37,050
But y'know, Hinase was so pure. If anyone
was in trouble, she'd always try to help.

223
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,050
You were such a sweetheart.

224
00:15:39,050 --> 00:15:41,840
So she's always been like that, huh?

225
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:44,560
Yeah, no, I'm nothing that special.

226
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:48,550
Hey, I know. I've still got our yearbook—

227
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:50,470
Didn't we come to play with the dog?

228
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:54,420
You're right. Sorry, sorry.

229
00:15:55,770 --> 00:15:59,500
Hotaru, these people are my friends.

230
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:02,780
C-Come here, Hotaru!

231
00:16:07,430 --> 00:16:10,450
Don't startle her. Just try to be gentle.

232
00:16:11,610 --> 00:16:14,760
Kyo-chan! I'll try going first.

233
00:16:15,430 --> 00:16:16,570
Up we go.

234
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:27,150
Kyo-chan!

235
00:16:27,630 --> 00:16:28,770
See? It's okay!

236
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:37,700
It's Hotaru, it's Hotaru,
it's Hotaru, it's Hotaru!

237
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:38,650
You mean me?

238
00:16:48,770 --> 00:16:51,160
Th-This might actually be okay.

239
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:52,120
Right?

240
00:16:52,670 --> 00:16:56,090
Hananoi, why don't you 
come pet Hotaru too?

241
00:16:57,130 --> 00:16:58,130
I'm good.

242
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:02,400
C'mon, don't be like that.

243
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:14,350
There, there.

244
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,770
You're a good girl, Hotaru.

245
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:23,900
<i>I feel like I'm watching 
something I shouldn't be.</i>

246
00:17:30,690 --> 00:17:33,410
Hey, I think I'm getting used to this.

247
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:35,780
Really? I'm so glad.

248
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:37,820
We can thank Yao-kun for that.

249
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:38,980
Yup.

250
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:43,400
You too, Hotaru. Thanks.

251
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:49,630
All this for a friend, huh?

252
00:17:49,630 --> 00:17:52,330
Hinase really is a good person.

253
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:55,080
"Hinase"?

254
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:55,820
Huh?

255
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:59,180
You're the one who told me
not to call her Hotako.

256
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:03,350
I mean, she's asked me that before, too.

257
00:18:04,410 --> 00:18:10,240
She's so nice, but she hates me.
 I wonder what I did wrong.

258
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,200
She say anything to you?

259
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,320
I don't know anything.

260
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:16,570
Oh, okay.

261
00:18:16,890 --> 00:18:21,740
Say, you know what? I feel like I've heard 
the name Hananoi somewhere before.

262
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:24,090
Have we meet before or something?

263
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,190
Who knows?

264
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:40,460
It looked like Kyo-chan was able 
to get over her fear a little. I'm so glad.

265
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,520
You do seem happy.

266
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,570
Yeah!

267
00:18:43,570 --> 00:18:45,810
Kyo-chan was thrilled, so I am too.

268
00:18:46,270 --> 00:18:49,060
I've got to find a way to thank Yao-kun.

269
00:18:49,790 --> 00:18:51,610
I'm a little jealous.

270
00:18:51,610 --> 00:18:52,470
Huh?

271
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:57,730
You really went out of your way for Asami-san.

272
00:18:57,730 --> 00:18:59,850
She must be over the moon.

273
00:18:59,850 --> 00:19:01,850
I-It was no big deal.

274
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:07,780
You don't think so? Most people wouldn't 
go so far to help a friend.

275
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:15,370
I mean, honestly, she's always been
the one helping <i>me</i> out.

276
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:21,040
Didn't Kyo-chan mention it? 
I was pretty gloomy in middle school.

277
00:19:21,950 --> 00:19:26,240
After what happened in elementary school, 
I was too scared to make friends.

278
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:30,560
I tried to keep to myself.

279
00:19:33,210 --> 00:19:36,980
That's when I met Kyo-chan.

280
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:45,220
I was actually a little scared to hang out 
with someone who was so open about love.

281
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:54,360
But for whatever reason,
 I had so much fun when I was with her.

282
00:19:55,730 --> 00:19:59,170
After a while, even though I 
still didn't understand it,

283
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:05,890
the idea of falling head over heels in love
started to sound so nice.

284
00:20:11,350 --> 00:20:18,570
If it weren't for Kyo-chan, I might never 
have wanted to try falling in love myself.

285
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,740
I'm never much help when we have girl talk,

286
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:27,700
so I'm really glad I was 
able to help her today!

287
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:31,320
Thank you for everything
 today too, Hananoi-kun.

288
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:34,520
Right...

289
00:20:35,730 --> 00:20:41,140
<i>So it was Asami-san who was there
for Hotaru-chan when she was at her lowest.</i>

290
00:20:42,310 --> 00:20:45,390
<i>I can't really compete with that.</i>

291
00:20:47,410 --> 00:20:50,910
Anyway, Hotaru sure was a cutey.

292
00:20:50,910 --> 00:20:53,470
Oh! I-I mean the dog!

293
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:58,980
Everyone was all "Hotaru this, Hotaru that"
 today. It started to feel weird.

294
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:01,610
<i>Like when you...</i>

295
00:21:01,610 --> 00:21:03,990
Er, forget I said that!

296
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:14,360
There, there. To me, you'll always be 
the best girl, Hotaru-chan.

297
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:19,900
Th-That's not what I meant!

298
00:21:20,810 --> 00:21:22,080
Now you're blushing!

299
00:22:53,010 --> 00:22:55,020
Year 6, Class 1

300
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:58,520
Hinase Hotaru

301
00:22:55,710 --> 00:23:00,360
It's been ages since I saw 
her smile like she used to.

302
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:01,770
Otowa Municipal South Elementary School, Otowa City

303
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:01,770
Graduation Album

304
00:23:07,190 --> 00:23:09,260
Wait, is that...

305
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:18,350
<i>I can't stand it.</i>

306
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:21,950
<i>Back then, why did I...?</i>

307
00:23:34,010 --> 00:23:36,020
Year 6, Class 5

